[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:The End of a Dream]
[00:12.97]How did the dream end?
[00:17.51]Tired of sleeping on the floor,
[00:20.60]a young man in Teheran saved up for years to buy a real bed.
[00:28.15]For the first time in his life,
[00:30.77]he became the proud owner of a bed which had springs and a mattress.
[00:38.51]Because the weather was very hot,
[00:41.53]he carried the bed on to the roof of his house.
[00:46.17]He slept very well for the first two nights,
[00:49.84]but on the third night, a storm blew up.
[00:54.60]A gust of wind swept the bed off the roof and sent it crashing into the courtyard below.
[01:04.09]The young man did not wake up until the bed had struck the ground.
[01:10.78]Although the bed was smashed to pieces,
[01:13.59]the man was miraculously unhurt.
[01:17.65]When he woke up, he was still on the mattress.
[01:22.72]Glancing at the bits of wood and metal that lay around him,
[01:27.36]the man sadly picked up the mattress and carried it into his house.
[01:33.82]After he had put it on the floor, he promptly went to sleep again.
